---
description: Non-negotiable backend rules for this project
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- Every table is org_id-scoped. Postgres RLS is the real boundary — enforce it with
  FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY, not just application-side filtering. Never write a query
  that filters by org_id in Python as the ONLY protection.
- RBAC checks happen server-side in service.py / deps.py, never trust a role or org_id
  claim the client sends as a plain argument — only trust it from the verified JWT.
- Every create/update/delete/status-transition on a core entity writes to activity_log
  with a before/after diff. Soft delete only (deleted_at) — never a hard DELETE on core
  entities. Repository reads must filter deleted_at IS NULL by default.
- All config comes from app/core/config.py's Settings object. Never call os.environ
  directly anywhere else, never hardcode a secret, connection string, or API key.
- One-to-many GraphQL fields (company.contacts, project.tasks, etc.) must use a
  DataLoader / batched query — no N+1 resolvers.
- Layering per module: models.py (Pydantic) -> repository.py (SQLAlchemy) ->
  service.py (business rules, state machines) -> schema.py (Strawberry, thin).
- GROQ calls are advisory only: wrap in try/except, degrade to null on failure or
  timeout, never block a business transaction on them, never write AI output into a
  field that represents a human decision or a computed number.
- See AGENTS.md at repo root for the data model, enums, actors, and state machines.
